          "notes": "Consolidated from HackRF_Power_Cal_Attenuator.xlsx, HackRF_Power_Cal_Remaining.xlsx and the shipped calibration.json. All values referred to the SDR input connector with the 10 dB pad fitted, so SigGen -40 dBm delivers -50 dBm - inside the linear window proven by D_Compression (-60/-50/-40 all give the same base at 2400 MHz; hard compression from -30 dBm). MEASURED anchors: 70, 100, 500, 1000, 2000, 2200, 2450, 2650, 2725, 3000, 5000 MHz. 3500-5800 MHz filled from H_Resweep's SHAPE lifted by a constant 10.63 dB (its offset vs consensus is 10.96/10.46/10.48 dB at 2200/2750/3000, so the shape is good even though its absolute level is not). 200-1800 MHz filled by log-frequency interpolation, because H_Resweep's low band ran at -32 dBm and was saturated. H_Resweep's absolute levels are EXCLUDED throughout: they disagree with all five other datasets by ~25 dB, and they are the sole source of the currently shipped power_base_offset_table, which should be re-measured. Gain block at rows 33+ from C_VGA_Check: VGA 0 is +5.86 dB off nominal, VGA 62 is -1.24 dB, VGA 10/30/40/50 nominal. FREQ_CAL rows are back-derived from the stored -297.7 Hz / 8.9304 ppm fit, not fresh bench readings. Re-measure the interpolated frequencies and FREQ_CAL to make this traceable rather than reconstructed.",
